WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.180
"American Pickers" is a classic staple of
reality TV.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.140
The History series has been around since 2010
and featured “friends” — more on this

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.269
later — Frank Fritz and Mike Wolfe traveling
around the country buying antiques and selling

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:13.669
them for a tidy profit.

00:00:13.669 --> 00:00:17.850
The business-within-a-show where all of the
action happens is known as Antique Archaeology,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:22.480
and Danielle Colby runs the whole operation,
while Fritz and Wolfe seek out all those juicy,

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.830
profitable treasures that fans eagerly tune
in to see.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:30.590
Season 22 started up with a new cast member,
Jersey Jon, and not Frank, joining Mike on

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.910
his back road adventures.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.820
The whole issue boiled over into public view
after Fritz confirmed that he would not be

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.840
returning to "American Pickers" despite concluding
his stint in rehab to treat alcohol addiction.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.190
In that same bombshell interview, Fritz divulged
that he and Wolfe had not spoken in years

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.730
even though he described their previous relationship
as close enough to "finish each other's sentences."

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.539
Wolfe later added fuel to the fire of speculation
with a social media post that confirmed Fritz

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:56.769
would not be returning to "American Pickers."

00:00:56.769 --> 00:01:00.530
That announcement was couched in effusive
statements of praise and affection:

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.110
"I will miss Frank, just like all of you,
and I pray for the very best and all good

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.160
things for him on the next part of his journey."

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.030
Colby, who is obviously in the middle of everything,
hasn't had much to say about the changes made

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.530
around her workplace — until now, that is.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.620
She broke her silence with a long, emotional
Instagram post.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.820
She had a lot to say, yet seemed to say almost
nothing of substance about the interpersonal

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.250
feud tearing apart her show — unless you
read between the lines.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.520
She rattles off a string of platitudes without
offering much context like,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.890
"You can only be where you are.”...“Sometimes
you just have to be okay with being apart."

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.520
And, "Walk in peace and lead with love."

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.410
Many fans believe that the post is an elliptical
reference to all the behind-the-scenes drama

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.110
that has overwhelmed her business and her
reality show.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.990
Most of the commentary is vague enough that
fans can read into whatever they want.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:49.480
That said, Colby's silence on the whole shakeup
has been deafening, so this seems like a potentially

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:52.990
deft way to weigh in without coming down hard
on either side.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.730
The post appears as deeply personal as it
is vague.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:02:00.160
She doesn't name any names or state any specifics,
so it's unclear whether she's talking about

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.350
herself or perhaps referencing the rift between
her co-stars.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.880
Based on what we know about their split, though,
there are some inferences we could make to

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.299
bridge the gap between her words and the situation.

00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:13.340
Here's some of the missing context from Colby's
post: The Sun also reported that over the

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.859
two years Wolfe and Fritz weren't speaking,
many months of which were during the height

00:02:16.859 --> 00:02:21.489
of the COVID-19 pandemic, Fritz was admitted
into rehab to combat a substance abuse problem.

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:26.290
He lost 65 pounds, had serious back surgery,
and is finally getting a leg up on his Crohn's

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.290
Disease.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.560
During all of that time, though, Wolfe never
bothered to reach out to check in and see

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:31.840
if he was okay.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.870
These details seem to frame Wolfe as the villain
of this particular story, and many fans hoped

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:39.239
that Colby's take might clarify who's in the
right and who's in the wrong.

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:42.930
That obviously didn't happen, and the one
thing that remains true about this interpersonal

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.069
saga is that we-the-public clearly don't have
a complete picture of the falling out between

00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:48.440
these two friends.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.870
So is Colby's post a letter to Fritz, letting
him know that he is still loved, even in his

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.870
absence?

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.860
Or is it more of a goodbye, encouraging him
to be strong on his own even though he's no

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.480
longer a part of the show?

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.629
It's really hard to say.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:03.760
But her words seem kind and encouraging, so
maybe there's hope to resolve things and see

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.939
both men working together again, even if Fritz
only makes the occasional appearance in lieu

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:10.129
of returning as co-host.

